        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b3d0a0baad71433cbe7470e4680b1a2c",
      "statement": "run_update parses the installed version from env!(CARGO_PKG_VERSION), prints the installed version and channel, and on an available update prints the version as stable or prerelease plus the latest stable release as context and an installation link, exiting 2 unless --check is set.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main.rs#L623-L696",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6d977d69815f484d4db8ba58c06d7562e9b802823d5d900de96f51aa15ebedbc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_85b17b0c7afc43cd927d897af8dcff92",
      "statement": "Unit tests pin the channel-aware behavior: a Stable-channel user at the newest stable is up to date even when a newer prerelease exists, a real newer stable is still offered on Stable, Stable falls back to overall when no stable exists, and Beta is up to date when the installed prerelease equals the newest release.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/update.rs#L509-L583",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e3a7fe88f684e66f58ca8829d04ac2b533aa630b7fe191da54b9a29f3a78dd29:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f200b93941334ac3ab139c0a1170ab51",
      "statement": "The update-check cache lives at update-check.json beside the config file (XDG resolution stays in one place), stores checked_at and the newest stable version, and is written atomically; missing, unreadable, or malformed caches all read back as None via a degrade-silently contract.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/update.rs#L232-L280",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:357d75e033c8861ac83807e925f32555a743af834c0748af32b8aad8c112d9d3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d60a779de3e140c5ad6b8ac86a73ce91",
      "statement": "On a successful `claudebar update`, the cache always records the newest stable release independent of the reported channel; when no stable release exists nothing is recorded, so stable-channel users are never badged toward a prerelease.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main.rs#L655-L660",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:33f6ed568764db97abaf1f365b9e4e3454992f73b096805a596185fe65e8d03f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_09f779d258734c83879ebbe4b9cb1bea",
      "statement": "On a failed fetch run_update still stamps the cache with the current time and the already-known newest version, so a background refresh backs off for a day instead of retrying every render and the badge is not blanked for machines offline when the daily refresh fires.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main.rs#L637-L654",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db9ba2b447666cb2f7e400af22750beb2fd168731c6f37cc57ccc1bf2de515cd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ba13c6ff48bf4afeba3ab97baf186851",
      "statement": "refresh_in_background only spawns a detached `update --check` child when the cache is missing or older than a day (REFRESH_INTERVAL = 86400 s); it claims the rate-limit slot by re-stamping the cache with the known version before the child's network call, the caller never waits on the child or sees its output, and nothing is spawned when no cache can be written.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/update.rs#L218-L219",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dba489afdf450d8cf6bd812c3c41c1d87c84e127f69d1e4dfbeafe999e2c9b6d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/update.rs#L282-L331",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c0e2d9465823c4582b7179402f8929f8a7c23e06b4203e560030e4aa0fff2d55:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2a3cbb23a4a94213975779cb0659de20",
      "statement": "render_line reads the update cache once and calls refresh_in_background when the update-notice segment is enabled, so the badge stays current without the render ever blocking on the network; when update-notice is disabled no cache read happens at all.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/render/mod.rs#L111-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a056d2283373467aa0799bdc44790a349ab6558a6464b2463e44c24773016160:"
        },
        {
